      "content": "The Utrecht sodomy trials (Dutch: \"Utrechtse sodomieprocessen\") were a large-scale persecution of homosexuals that took place in the Dutch Republic, starting in the city of Utrecht in 1730. Over the following year, the persecution of \"sodomites\" spread to the rest of the nation, leading to some 250 to 300 trials, often ending in a death sentence.",
